1
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:34,800
You are not welcome here.

2
00:08:57,600 --> 00:09:03,600
District 9 is a science fiction film directed by Neill Blomkamp.

3
00:13:26,400 --> 00:13:32,400
Thirty years ago, aliens arrive on Earth.

4
00:17:55,200 --> 00:18:01,200
Not to conquer or give aid, but to find refuge from their dying planet.

5
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:30,000
Separated from humans in a South African area called District 9, the aliens are managed by Multi-National United,
which is unconcerned with the aliens' welfare but will do anything to master their advanced technology.

6
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:58,800
When a company field agent contracts a mysterious virus that begins to alter
his DNA, there is only one place he can hide: District 9.

7
00:31:21,600 --> 00:31:27,600
Wikus van de Merwe, played by Sharlto Copley.

8
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:56,400
Christopher Johnson / Grey Bradnam / Trent, played by Jason Cope.

9
00:40:19,200 --> 00:40:25,200
Sarah Livingstone - Sociologist, played by Nathalie Boltt.

10
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:54,000
Dr Katrina McKenzie, played by Sylvaine Strike.

11
00:49:16,800 --> 00:49:22,800
Interviewee, played by Elizabeth Mkandawie.

12
00:53:45,600 --> 00:53:51,600
Les Feldman - MIL Engineer, played by John Sumner.

13
00:58:14,400 --> 00:58:20,400
District 9 is a 2009 science fiction action film
directed and co-written by Neill Blomkamp.

14
01:02:43,200 --> 01:02:49,200
It was a co-production of New Zealand, the United States, and South Africa.

15
01:07:12,000 --> 01:07:18,000
The film stars Sharlto Copley, Jason Cope, and David James, and was
adapted from Blomkamp's 2005 short film Alive in Joburg.

16
01:11:40,800 --> 01:11:46,800
The film is partially presented in a mock documentary format by featuring
fictional interviews, news footage, and video from surveillance cameras.

17
01:16:09,600 --> 01:16:15,600
The story, which explores themes of humanity, xenophobia and social segregation, begins in an
alternate 1982, when an alien spaceship appears over Johannesburg, South Africa.

18
01:20:38,400 --> 01:20:44,400
When a population of sick and malnourished insectoid aliens is discovered on the ship, the
South African government confines them to an internment camp called District 9.

19
01:25:07,199 --> 01:25:13,199
The title and premise of District 9 were inspired by events in
Cape Town's District Six, during the apartheid era.

20
01:29:36,000 --> 01:29:42,000
District 9 premiered on 23 July 2009 at San Diego Comic-Con, and was released in New Zealand on 13
August, the United States on 14 August and South Africa on 28 August, by TriStar Pictures.

21
01:34:04,800 --> 01:34:10,800
It received positive reviews from critics, and was a financial
success, earning $211 million on a budget of $30 million.

22
01:38:33,600 --> 01:38:39,600
It garnered numerous award nominations, including Academy Awards for Best Picture,
Best Adapted Screenplay, Best Visual Effects, and Best Film Editing.

23
01:43:02,400 --> 01:43:08,400
The film explores themes of street gang, government, genetics, slum, mutation.

24
01:47:31,200 --> 01:47:37,200
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
